        "title": "Contemporary Furniture Design and Digital Fabrication",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The most significant shift in contemporary furniture is the collapse of the gap between design and production. CNC tools mean that an individual with a design file can produce a custom chair; digital files can be shared globally; and the economics of manufacturing are no longer exclusively dominated by large factory runs."
